## Approach

Build an index of provider coordinates by specialty. For each member, check each required specialty in turn for a provider whose squared distance is not greater than d^2. The time is O(P+M*R*P_s), where P_s is the number of providers with the relevant specialty.

## Proof of correctness

A member is adequately served if and only if each required specialty has at least one provider within the distance limit. The algorithm checks this existence specialty by specialty; as soon as one is missing, the member is added to the result. Sorting at the end only affects the display order.

## Complexity

Coordinates are integers, so squared distances can be compared to avoid floating-point error; the distance bound includes being equal to maxDistance.

O(P + M*R*P) time and O(P) space, where R is the number of specialties a member requires.

## Reference implementation

```python
def solve(raw):
 z=raw.splitlines();P,M,d=map(int,z[0].split());by={}
 for line in z[1:1+P]:
  i,s,x,y=line.split();by.setdefault(s,[]).append((int(x),int(y)))
 ans=[]
 for line in z[1+P:1+P+M]:
  mid,x,y,req=line.split();x=int(x);y=int(y);bad=False
  for s in req.split('|'):
   if not any((a-x)**2+(b-y)**2<=d*d for a,b in by.get(s,[])):bad=True;break
  if bad:ans.append(int(mid))
 return '\n'.join(map(str,sorted(ans)))
```
